# Teach by Example: "When you next cast an instant or sorcery spell this turn, copy that spell." Only YOUR instant or sorcery
# spell is the next one (CR 603.7b): Bot1 resolves it on turn 3, then casts Ornithopter (a creature spell) and Bot2 answers with its
# own Lightning Bolt at Bot1 - neither is copied and the delayed ability stays. Bot1's Lightning Bolt is copied, and Bot1 keeps the
# target (CR 707.10c, "may"): the copy and the Bolt both hit Bot2 for 6. The copy is not cast (CR 707.10), so nothing else triggers.

